  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1203 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nA short-waved trough is expected to brush the area \nMonday night into Tuesday. However, not expecting any impacts other \nthan delaying the warming of temperatures further, until Wed when \nupper level ridging is expected to build and bring temperatures to \nthe upper 70s and potentially some lower 80s Wed into Thu. With this \nshortwave, PoPs remain less than 10 at the moment, but would not \ncompletely rule out some isolated showers early morning through the \nday. The next potential system to bring temperatures back down along \nwith decent rain chances is not expected until Thursday night into \nFriday at this time. Temperatures may not cool quite as much, \ndepending on how the next trough comes across and how much rain \ncomes with it as well. For now, the NBM is giving temperatures for \nFriday and Saturday very similar to Thursday, but this may change \nand temperatures may come it a few degrees cooler.",
